Drop-6 tooth-coordinate proof view
  Normalize the omitted speed-6 tooth centered at 1/6 by
    x = 14*6*(t - 1/6), so the tooth is [-1,1].
  A speed v with center j/v contributes
    [14*(6*j-v)/v - 6/v, 14*(6*j-v)/v + 6/v].
    v=13, j= 2, defect=-1, center=-14/13, half=6/13, interval=[-20/13,-8/13], clipped=[-1,-8/13]
    v=12, j= 2, defect= 0, center=0, half=1/2, interval=[-1/2,1/2], clipped=[-1/2,1/2]
    v=11, j= 2, defect= 1, center=14/11, half=6/11, interval=[8/11,20/11], clipped=[8/11,1]
  merged clipped cover=[(Fraction(-1, 1), Fraction(-8, 13)), (Fraction(-1, 2), Fraction(1, 2)), (Fraction(8, 11), Fraction(1, 1))]
  uncovered x-components=[(Fraction(-8, 13), Fraction(-1, 2)), (Fraction(1, 2), Fraction(8, 11))]
  x-length=49/143; t-length in this tooth=7/1716
  The opposite tooth k=5 is the global reflection of this one.

