Conclusion
  The current worst core is not just AP13 minus 6; it is a D6
  missing-clock shadow.  Its measure is the sum of two reflected
  endpoint-mouth orbits, both inside the omitted speed-6 moat:
    2*(1/728) + 2*(5/1848) = 7/858.
  In the tested two-delete/one-replacement family, any attempt to
  damage those old hexagon mouths forces enough new reflected mouth
  mass elsewhere; the smallest surplus over drop6 is 1/980 and occurs
  without damaging the old mouths.  This suggests the next proof target:
  a dihedral mouth-exchange inequality for coordinated growth.
